cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use leather in research, cite it as below."
type: software
title: "leather: local agent infrastructure in one stdlib-only Go binary"
authors:
  - family-names: Pate
    given-names: Tyler
    alias: TGPSKI
version: 0.5.4
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22637736
date-released: "2026-09-07"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22637735
    description: "Concept DOI, resolves to the latest release"
license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/TGPSKI/leather"
url: "https://leather.sh"
abstract: >-
  A single Go binary, no dependencies outside the standard library, that runs
  declarative agents on a workstation, server, or Raspberry Pi: scheduled jobs,
  one-shot runs, webhook-driven workflows, tool calling, and auditable run
  records. The repository includes examples/14-sig-triage, an evaluation
  campaign that measures how much of a small local model's task accuracy is
  determined by the runtime around it, with the weights and hardware held
  fixed.
keywords:
  - agents
  - LLM runtime
  - local inference
  - tool calling
  - Go
  - evaluation
